<title>USA: Morgan Stanley details U.S. portfolio adjustment.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley details U.S. portfolio adjustment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley on Wednesday said U.S. equity strategist Byron Wien removed four stocks from his model U.S. portfolio as part of an adjustment that included an addition of three percentage points to the portfolio's cash position.</p>
<p>A Morgan Stanley spokeswoman said Wien deleted one percent positions in Silicon Graphics Inc, Exide Corp, Pronet Inc and Hercules Inc.</p>
<p>A one percent position in Corning Inc was added, leaving the U.S. model portfolio with a 92 percent investment in equities and an eight percent cash position.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
